Virtual Assistance and Appointment Setter Cohort 2: Full Curriculum
Vixora Academy · 8 weeks · Draft v1 for review
Course Overview
This practical course trains students to work as professional virtual assistants and appointment setters. Students learn the admin, communication and productivity skills clients pay for, how to use AI tools to work faster, and how to find leads and book sales calls through outreach. The course ends with a portfolio, a set of service packages and a plan to land the first client.
* Duration: 8 weeks
* Format: Online / Physical (hybrid)
* Level: Beginner (no experience required)
* Pricing: ₦30,000
* Certificate: Awarded on completion of the final project
Learning Outcomes
By the end of the course, students will be able to:
* Explain what virtual assistants and appointment setters do, and choose a niche
* Communicate professionally with clients in writing and on calls
* Manage email, calendars and tasks for a client
* Use Google Workspace, Notion, Trello and similar tools
* Use AI tools to draft, summarize, schedule and organize
* Manage leads in a simple CRM
* Run cold outreach by email, LinkedIn and phone using clear scripts
* Handle objections and book qualified calls
* Find clients, set rates and onboard them professionally
Tools Used
Google Workspace (Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets), Notion, Trello, Calendly or similar scheduling tools, a free or low-cost CRM, AI assistants (ChatGPT, Claude and similar), LinkedIn, and basic communication tools such as Zoom and Slack. Free versions are used wherever possible.
Course Structure
* Phase 1: Foundations (Weeks 1-2): career paths, professional communication, admin tools
* Phase 2: Core VA Skills (Weeks 3-4): email and calendar management, AI tools for virtual assistants
* Phase 3: Appointment Setting (Weeks 5-7): CRM and lead management, cold outreach and scripts, objection handling and booking calls
* Phase 4: Business and Career (Week 8): finding clients, rates, onboarding and portfolio
Assessment (Proposed)
* Weekly practical assignments
* Mock client tasks (inbox, calendar and task management)
* Mock appointment-setting call and outreach set
* Final project: a service package, an outreach campaign plan and a portfolio
* Certificate issued on completing all weekly deliverables and the final project
Week 1: Introduction to Virtual Assistance, Career Paths and Professional Communication
Objectives
* Understand the VA and appointment setter roles
* Communicate like a professional
Topics
* What virtual assistants do: admin, customer support, social media, bookkeeping support, appointment setting
* Remote work basics and the client relationship
* Choosing a niche (for example real estate, coaching, e-commerce, health and wellness, tech and AI businesses)
* Professional email writing and tone
* Meeting etiquette and video call basics
* Time zones, response times and reliability
Hands-on
* Write a professional introduction email and a short niche statement
* Role-play a first call with a client
Deliverable: niche statement and a professional email pack
Week 2: Productivity and Admin Tools
Objectives
* Set up and use the tools clients expect
* Organize work and files clearly
Topics
* Google Workspace: Drive, Docs, Sheets and sharing permissions
* Notion: pages, databases and simple client dashboards
* Trello: boards, lists, cards and task tracking
* Naming files and organizing folders
* Time tracking and daily workflow
Hands-on
* Set up a complete mock client workspace with a task board and shared folders
Deliverable: mock client workspace
Week 3: Email, Calendar and Inbox Management
Objectives
* Manage a busy inbox and calendar for a client
* Schedule without conflicts
Topics
* Inbox management: labels, filters, folders and the inbox-zero routine
* Writing and using email templates
* Calendar management, scheduling rules and time zones
* Scheduling tools such as Calendly
* Travel and meeting coordination
* Confidentiality and handling sensitive information
Hands-on
* Process a mock inbox of 50 emails and schedule a week of meetings for a mock client
Deliverable: organized mock inbox and calendar, with a short handover note
Week 4: AI Tools for Virtual Assistants
Objectives
* Use AI to work faster without lowering quality
* Check AI output before sending it to clients
Topics
* Prompting AI assistants for emails, summaries and reports
* Meeting notes, transcription and action items
* Research and data entry with AI
* Drafting social posts and simple documents
* Scheduling and task automation tools
* Client privacy: what never goes into an AI tool
Hands-on
* Complete a set of VA tasks with AI help and a short check of each result
Deliverable: AI-assisted task pack with a prompt list
Week 5: CRM Basics and Lead Management
Objectives
* Track leads and follow-ups in a CRM
* Build a clean lead list
Topics
* What a CRM is and why clients need one
* Setting up a simple CRM (pipeline stages, contacts and notes)
* Finding and organizing leads: LinkedIn, directories and lead tools
* Qualifying leads: who is a good prospect
* Follow-up schedules and reminders
* Data accuracy and basic data privacy
Hands-on
* Build a lead list of 30 prospects in a CRM with pipeline stages
Deliverable: CRM with a qualified lead list
Week 6: Cold Outreach and Scripts
Objectives
* Reach prospects by email, LinkedIn and phone
* Write outreach that gets replies
Topics
* How appointment setting works and what clients expect
* Cold email: subject lines, structure and follow-ups
* LinkedIn outreach: profile, connection notes and messages
* Cold call basics and call scripts
* Personalizing at scale, with AI help
* Rules and ethics: consent, spam laws and honesty
Hands-on
* Write an outreach sequence for one niche across email, LinkedIn and call
Deliverable: outreach sequence and call script
Week 7: Handling Objections and Booking Calls
Objectives
* Respond calmly to objections
* Book qualified calls and hand them over properly
Topics
* Common objections: not interested, no time, send me information, too expensive
* Listening, acknowledging and responding
* Qualifying questions
* Booking the call: confirmation, reminders and reducing no-shows
* Handing over a lead with clear notes
* Tracking results: reply rate, booking rate and show rate
Hands-on
* Complete role-played setter calls with feedback
* Practice objection responses
Deliverable: recorded or live mock call and an objection-handling sheet
Week 8: Finding Clients, Rates, Onboarding and Portfolio
Objectives
* Land the first client
* Run the business side professionally
Topics
* Where to find clients: LinkedIn, freelance platforms, referrals and local businesses
* Service packages: VA support and appointment setting
* Pricing models: hourly, monthly retainer and per booked call
* Proposals, simple contracts and invoices
* Client onboarding: questionnaire, access and communication rules
* Building a portfolio and a LinkedIn profile
* Final project presentations
Hands-on
* Write service packages and a client onboarding checklist
* Present the final project
Deliverable: service packages, onboarding checklist, portfolio and final project
Final Project Requirements (Proposed)
* A niche statement and ideal client profile
* Two or three service packages with pricing
* A lead list of at least 30 prospects in a CRM
* An outreach campaign: email, LinkedIn message and call script
* A client onboarding checklist
* A portfolio page or document
* A 5-minute presentation and a mock call